/// NodeShapeSkew — system event announced when a class shared with a
/// connected peer has a different `shapeVersion` there (ADR 0126 §5.3,
/// Phase 4).
///
/// Published on `SystemAnnouncer current` by the runtime's
/// `beamtalk_node_monitor`: once when a peer connects (comparing its shape
/// manifest, fetched via `erpc`, against this node's own), and again
/// whenever a shared class is hot-reloaded on this node while peers are
/// connected. This is an early-warning, non-gating signal — version skew
/// between connected nodes is expected during a rolling upgrade (ADR
/// 0125); a per-message wire send still enforces the strict version check
/// (`shape_version_ahead`, ADR 0126 §5.2) independently of this event.
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// SystemAnnouncer current when: NodeShapeSkew do: [:e |
///   Transcript showLine: e className asString ++ " skewed with " ++ e node name asString
/// ]
/// ```
sealed typed Announcement subclass: NodeShapeSkew
  field: node :: Node
  field: className :: Symbol
  field: localVersion :: Integer
  field: remoteVersion :: Integer
